' 06a Lifecycle of a space transaction, as a state machine.
'
' Source of Figure S5.2a in ../design.md (section S5.2). The diagram plan
' numbers this figure 06a, a sub-figure of figure 06.
' The figure restates SpaceStoreHandle::begin, TxnRegistration, HostTxn and
' its commit, and the begin of each host, in rspace++/src/rspace/
' space_store_handle.rs, rspace/space_play.rs and
' replay_rspace/space_replay.rs. It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. begin registers the task, checks the lock keys, and takes the stripes.
'   2. In the Open state the agent reads and stages. A rejected staging keeps
'      the transaction open. A failed view change closes it.
'   3. A drop ends the transaction with no effect. A commit ends it with the
'      receipts, or with an error that has no effect or leaves a prefix.
'   4. Every state after the end releases the locks and the registration,
'      and a later call fails with Finished.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 06a-space-txn-lifecycle.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 06a-space-txn-lifecycle
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam StateBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title Lifecycle of a space transaction (figure 06a)

state "Registering" as REG $rrs_substrate : SpaceStoreHandle::begin(lock keys)\nregister the current task or thread\nin the handle (FR-9)
state "Locking" as LOCK $rrs_host : SpaceTxnHost::begin\nconsume_lock: the phase-A stripes,\nthen the phase-B stripes, ascending
state "Open" as OPEN $rrs_substrate {
  state "Reading" as READ $rrs_substrate : data, continuations, joins,\nproduce_counters, recorded_comms, admits\nfirst touch reads through the history trie
  state "Staging" as STAGE $rrs_substrate : produce or consume with an outcome\nvalidate, compute the COMM\n<latex>\mathit{times}(p) = \kappa_v(p) + [\neg \mathit{persist} \wedge p = \mathit{src}]</latex>\nverify in replay, apply to the view
  [*] --> READ
  READ --> STAGE : stage
  STAGE --> READ : staged, or rejected\nwith no effect
  READ --> READ : read
}
state "Committing" as COMMITTING $rrs_substrate : operation i runs under\n<latex>\mathit{parent} \mathbin{+\!\!+} [(i, 2)]</latex>\nread-only checks, host calls,\nevent correlation
state "Committed" as DONE $rrs_storage : the receipts are returned\nthe effects are in the hot store
state "Failed" as FAILED $rrs_reject : no effect: StoreSwapped, ParentOrderReused\nprefix: an error of operation i\nleaves operations 0 to i - 1 applied
state "Closed" as CLOSED $rrs_reject : a view change failed after validation\n(Inconsistent, a defect)\nno effect on the host
state "Dropped" as DROPPED $rrs_substrate : the agent dropped the transaction\nno event, no observer call, no write

[*] --> REG : begin(lock keys)
REG --> [*] : **NestedTransaction**\nthe task already holds a transaction\nor a sweep of this handle, no lock taken
state KEYS <<choice>>
REG --> KEYS : registered
KEYS --> [*] : **InvalidOperation**\nempty lock keys: no lock taken,\nregistration dropped
KEYS --> LOCK : lock keys present
LOCK --> OPEN : stripes held, hot store,\ninstalled set and lock coverage captured
OPEN --> CLOSED : view change fails
OPEN --> DROPPED : drop
OPEN --> COMMITTING : commit()
COMMITTING --> DONE : every operation applied
COMMITTING --> FAILED : an error
DONE --> [*] : release the locks,\nthen the registration
FAILED --> [*] : release the locks,\nthen the registration
CLOSED --> [*] : locks and registration\nreleased at once
DROPPED --> [*] : locks and registration\nreleased by drop

note right of DONE
After the end, every call on the
transaction fails with **Finished**.
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_substrate>  | state of the substrate |
|<$rrs_host>       | host lock acquisition (consume_lock) |
|<$rrs_storage>    | the effects reached the hot store |
|<$rrs_reject>     | failed or closed |
endlegend
@enduml
